    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "amd §3-300, Vil L",
    "lawSection": "Village Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6702\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the village law, in relation to permitting village\njustices of the village of Sag Harbor to live in the towns of East\nHampton or Southampton\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nPermits village justices of the village of Sag Harbor to live in the\ntowns of East Hampton or Southampton.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 3-300 of the village law is amended by adding a new\nsubdivision 18.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nUnder current law, the Village of Sag Harbor has two residency options\nfor village justices. The Village now requires the justice(s) to live\neither in the Village of Sag Harbor or within Suffolk County. This law\npresents some geographical issues in that the Village of Sag Harbor is\nonly 2 square miles and Suffolk County consists of 1,000 square miles.\nAccordingly, this presents problems for Sag Harbor Village in that the\ncandidate pool for qualified individuals seeking a position as a\nVillage Justice is either too small or too large.  Further, the\nVillage of Sag Harbor is located within the Town of Southampton and\nthe Town of East Hampton.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nS.3065 - 2007-08\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to state.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
